---
import Site from '../../layouts/Site.astro';
import PageHeader from '../../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { release, url } from '../../lib/publication';
const districts = release.geographies.filter(g => g.type === 'district');
---
<Site title="District evidence"><PageHeader title="Districts: the missing local layer" eyebrow="Geographic coverage" description="District reporting is valuable only when the place, boundary version and measurement mean the same thing. This publication has not approved a district series yet." />
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="atlas-coverage"><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Approved district entries</p><strong>{districts.length}</strong><p>A zero here is a count of published records, not a water condition.</p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">District rainfall readings</p><strong>{release.observations.filter(o => districts.some(d => d.id === o.geographyId)).length}</strong><p>No state or regional value is copied into a district.</p></div><div class="atlas-kpi"><p class="eyebrow">Current status</p><strong>Review</strong><p>Source and boundary matching are required before publication.</p></div></div>{districts.length ? <div class="table-wrap"><table class="data-table"><caption>Approved district records</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">District</th><th scope="col">Code</th><th scope="col">Approved observations</th></tr></thead><tbody>{districts.map(g => <tr><td>{g.name}</td><td>{g.code || 'Pending'}</td><td>{release.observations.filter(o => o.geographyId === g.id).length}</td></tr>)}</tbody></table></div> : <div class="note"><strong>No district conditions are reported here.</strong><p>India’s district names, splits and boundaries need a dated codebook. A rainfall map with ambiguous district labels would look precise while being difficult to verify.</p></div>}</div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="shell"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="eyebrow">Publication threshold</p><h2>Four checks before a district number appears</h2></div></div><ol class="grid-2 evidence-timeline"><li><h3>Identify the district</h3><p>Obtain a dated official administrative code and handle district splits and name changes.</p><a href={url('/sources/lgd/')}>LGD source lead ↗</a></li><li><h3>Match the measurement footprint</h3><p>Confirm the provider’s district boundary and station inventory for the period being shown.</p><a href={url('/sources/')}>Browse sources ↗</a></li><li><h3>Recheck the arithmetic</h3><p>Keep reported, derived and missing values separate. Do not reinterpret “No Data” as zero.</p><a href={url('/methodology/')}>Read the calculation rules ↗</a></li><li><h3>Preserve the source trail</h3><p>Ship the date, baseline, retrieval time and exact locator with every published row.</p><a href={url('/journalists/')}>Journalist exports ↗</a></li></ol></div></section></Site>
